  "title": "Sugary Drinks and Stomach Cancer: What a New Study Really Found",
  "summary": "A new study has raised concerns about a possible connection between sugary drinks and stomach cancer. Researchers analysing health and lifestyle data from more than 100,000 adults found that people who regularly consumed sugar-sweetened beverages appeared to have a higher risk of developing gastric cancer. The findings are significant because stomach cancer remains a major global health concern. However, the research does not prove that drinking sugary beverages directly causes cancer. Instead,",
